XFood:
X
XOnce you have mastered combat, you will find that food becomes the
Xmain problem. If you do not continually eat food, you will
eventually begin Xto faint and starve. Fainting is often enough to
kill a character by itself. X
XThe key is to hunt down food constantly. Hunt, kill and eat all the
Xedible creatures you can find. ALWAYS search for monsters which can
give Xyou special abilities. In particular, before continuing below
the second Xlevel you should find and eat, if possible, a leprechaun
and a floating Xeye. See my earlier comment on eating leprechauns.
X
XHowever, do not eat so much that you could not eat any more. The
Xreason is that if you are on the verge of choking, and kill, for
example, Xa wraith, you would not be able to eat the cadaver for a
long time, and so Xit might spoil before you get the chance.
X
XUnidentified items:
X
XYet another key point is to find out as quickly as possible which
Xitems have which powers. This does not mean, however, that you should
Xtry every item out the instant you get it.
X
XWe will deal with the different items separately.
X
XPotions:
X
XYou should almost never test out potions until you are at fith level
for Xwizards, or ninth level for other characters, at full hit points
and are on Xa cleared level. If you are not of those levels, you run
the risk of wasting Xa potion of gain level without gaining the
ability to teleport at will. Xonly if you have teleportitis. If you
are not at full hit points, then Xshould you quaff a healing potion,
it will not affect your maximum hit Xpoints. If there are creatures
nearby, you run the risk of being paralyzed Xor confused, and unable
to defend yourself. Lastly, always test your Xduplicate potions first.
X
XScrolls:
X
XYou should only test out scrolls when you are wearing a spare set of
Xarmor and are wielding a spare weapon. This allows you to not risk
your good Xequipment on determining which scrolls are the destroy
armor and damage Xweapon scrolls. Of course, once one of these have
been found, you no longer Xhave to take precautions against it. You
also should wait until you have Xsomething to identify, in case it is
an identify scroll. You won't have to Xwait long. And, as with
potions, check the duplicate scrolls first. X
XRings:
X
XRings should be identified first, since they are the hardest thing
Xto identify, aside from gems. Trying on unidentified rings is not
encouraged, Xas one cursed ring can ruin the game. If you have a
scroll of remove curse, Xit is safe to try on the ring. You can check
it out if there is a Nymph on Xthe level. That is dealt with later.
If you have several unidentified Xrings, (or armor or weapons) try
them all until you have on as many Xcursed items as possible. This
will allow you to de-curse as many as Xpossible with one scroll.
X
XWands:
X
XALWAYS test out wands as soon as there is a weak monster in your area
Xto zap them at. Since wand might shoot out a ray or a bolt, which
bounce, Xit is vitally important to shoot the wand diagnolly in such
a way that Xshould the bolt bounce, it will not hit the character.
The bolt is of a Xfinite length, so in a large room it may be safely
zapped in a straight Xline. Sometimes this is not a good idea. You
might get a polymorph wand Xand might polymorph that weak monster
into a dragon or other powerful Xmonster.
X
XUsually, the wand's function is now apparent. For wands, however,
this Xmay not be sufficient to identify the wand. After zapping such
a wand, and Xobserving the target, call the wand something such as
"tested1". This shows Xyou that, although its purpose is not known,
the wand has been used. If in XNetHack, you also could try to engrave
with the wand. This will identify Xa lot of wands. The others could
be identified by some other means. XYou can also engrave with the
wand, "E". The wands function should then Xbecome apparent.
X
